{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4vy69fxhmWdb6wGCXm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it with a one-line change in `django/db/models/sql/compiler.py:35`: the `ordering_parts` regex now has the `re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL` flags.\n\n```python\nself.ordering_parts = re.compile(r'(.*)\\s(ASC|DESC)(.*)', re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\n```\n\n**Cause:** without `DOTALL`, `.` doesn't match newlines. So for a multiline `RawSQL`, the regex only picked up the last line before `ASC`/`DESC`. Two different expressions that ended with the same line (like `else null end`) looked like duplicates, and the second was dropped from the `ORDER BY`.\n\n**Fix:** with `DOTALL`, `(.*)` captures the whole expression, newlines included. Duplicates are now judged on the full SQL, not just its last line.\n\nThe `expressions`, `ordering` and `queries` test modules pass (513 tests). I didn't add a test, because the rules don't allow editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":19551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c1b87c1-b878-4090-ae6b-deccadd37d76","uuid":"c521aca0-c0d0-4334-b04f-1f64e93526ae","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:26:38.737Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4vxvyR6kRT8HuRNPQE"}
